WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.177 --> 00:00:01.010
(tense tonal music)

00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:04.040
- [Narrator] This is an artist
painting a portrait of a cat.

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:06.080
She wasn't hired by this cat's owner,

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:09.110
but by Chewy, the online pet supply store.

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:11.470
The company has set out tens of thousands

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:14.860
of these surprise pet portraits
over the past eight years.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:16.290
And during the pandemic,

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:19.440
Chewy customers have shared
them across social media.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:23.180
The same time, the company's
business has been booming.

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:28.010
In 2020, Chewy gained over 5
1/2 million active customers.

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:30.520
- We took action pretty quickly,
actually, in our opinion,

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:34.400
and the strategy looking
back was really communicate,

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:35.890
innovate and persevere.

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:38.950
- [Narrator] Here's how Chewy
seized the pandemic pet craze

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:41.390
and ignited investor enthusiasm.

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:44.473
And why some analysts think
its success is built to last.

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:48.460
When the pandemic took hold in 2020,

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:51.020
millions of people were
forced to work from home

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:54.470
and with more time on their
hands, they adopted new pets.

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:56.900
Analysts estimate that
more than 11 million pets

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:58.950
found new homes during the pandemic.

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:01.050
And while pet owners were stuck at home,

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:03.760
many turned to the
internet to buy supplies.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:05.420
According to a recent report,

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:07.610
consumers bought 30% of their pet food

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:12.050
and supplies online last
year, up from 23% in 2019.

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:14.910
This added up to about $5 billion increase

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:16.820
in online pet spending.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:17.670
Laurent Schenk,

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:20.280
who analyzes the pet
industry for Morgan Stanley,

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:23.660
says this increase was a
big benefit for retailers.

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:26.800
- We do believe that the pet
industry is better positioned

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:28.640
than some other e-commerce categories

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:31.810
to retain the gains that it saw in 2020

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:33.510
given the sticky-like nature

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:35.890
of not only the product in pet food,

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:37.970
but also the customers themselves

00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:41.590
which tend to be very loyal
to specific retailers.

00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:43.670
- [Narrator] With the
influx of new pet owners,

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:45.500
retailers like Target and Amazon

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:48.140
all gained more shoppers
over the past year.

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:51.420
But sitting at the top
of the dog pile? Chewy.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:53.190
Morgan Stanley says the company

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:56.940
has the #1 market share
position for online pet retail.

00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:59.660
- Chewy has performed exceptionally well

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:01.480
during the pandemic,

00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:04.300
obviously a beneficiary of the shift

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:07.910
from offline to online as
it relates to e-commerce.

00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:08.930
But they also benefited

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:11.750
from the structural
increase in pet ownership.

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:14.610
- [Narrator] But Chewy's
success wasn't just timing.

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:16.260
Analysts say it had a lot to do

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:18.120
with how management at the company

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:20.990
handled the demand from
the pandemic pet boom.

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:24.940
When COVID-19 first first took
hold in the US in March 2020,

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:27.340
Chewy, like many other companies,

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:29.290
was overwhelmed with orders.

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:32.680
The surge in e-commerce demand
strained postal services

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:34.740
and this caused week-long delays

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:37.250
that put even more pressure on retailers.

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:39.560
Sumit Singh, the CEO of Chewy,

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:42.280
explains how this impacted his company.

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:44.740
- When industry-wide supply
chains were disrupted,

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:47.030
what was going on was that
we weren't receiving products

00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:48.930
optimally across the fulfillment center.

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:52.110
Number two, because fulfillment
center backlog was so high,

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:53.350
typically we deliver product

00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:55.660
between one and two days
to customers reliably.

00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:58.440
Our shipping times went
up to seven to 10 days.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:02.100
- [Narrator] Competitors like
Amazon faced similar issues.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:05.790
But at this key moment, Chewy
made strategic decisions.

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:07.600
To handle the increase in demand,

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:09.550
it hired thousands of new workers

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:10.640
while protecting shipments

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:12.920
for its core subscription customers.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:15.820
The company also invested
in shipping packages by air

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:17.810
to ensure timely delivery.

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:20.000
- Across a combination of
these three mechanisms,

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.370
we were able to sort of
control our situation.

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:24.160
- [Narrator] While these
investments were expensive,

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:25.890
Schenk says they were the right move.

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:28.130
- For businesses that can
retain these customers,

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:29.740
which we think Chewy can,

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:32.210
this should ultimately pay off dividends

00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:34.270
over the course of the next several years.

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:35.660
- [Narrator] Over the past year,

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:37.910
Chewy rolled out a number of new products

00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:39.860
with a focus on pet health.

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:41.930
In October, the company released

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:45.740
its own pet telehealth service
called Connect with a Vet.

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:48.440
The company's CEO says
the platform was launched

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:50.850
in response to the demand for vet care

00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:53.790
while clinics were impacted
by global shutdowns.

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:57.607
- We internally said, "Okay,
how about we develop a solution

00:03:57.607 --> 00:04:00.137
"that allows us to connect
customers and veterinarians

00:04:00.137 --> 00:04:01.380
"in a time of crisis?"

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:02.790
And we did exactly that.

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:03.810
- [Narrator] Chewy continued

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:05.980
to lean into its healthcare business.

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:08.370
The company announced that
it would be manufacturing

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:10.460
its own compounded medications,

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:13.460
which analysts say is a
competitive advantage.

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:15.850
But rolling out new products is expensive

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:18.120
and this cut into Chewy's profits.

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:20.320
Analysts say these product investments,

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:23.030
along with other
pandemic-related expenses,

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:24.330
are part of why the company

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.380
has yet to show an annual profit.

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:29.070
- Any time you make an investment, yes,

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:32.560
you're committing to
generating a healthy return

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:33.400
over the longterm.

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:35.240
And we are very longterm focused.

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:37.630
As it incidentally happens,
this particular service,

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:40.350
Connect with a Vet, yes, it
is currently a cost center

00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:41.660
because we're not monetizing it.

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:43.490
It's free for customers.

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:45.580
- [Narrator] Still,
analysts say some investors

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:46.750
have concerns.

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:48.820
- One of the things that investors

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:51.160
have also been a little
bit concerned about

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:55.990
is the fact that Chewy's
flow-through has been smaller,

00:04:55.990 --> 00:04:58.810
lighter than some other
e-commerce retailer's experience

00:04:58.810 --> 00:04:59.760
during the pandemic,

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:01.060
and I think part of that reason

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:03.970
was the incremental cleaning
costs and the shipping costs,

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:06.210
but also the fact that they did open

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:07.750
a new distribution center.

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:09.380
- [Narrator] The company's
stock saw pullback

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:10.790
over recent weeks.

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:12.210
- The cost that we've invested

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:15.130
in the health and safety
of our team members,

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:18.930
we are not looking to roll
those costs back 100%.

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:21.020
We believe 80% of those costs

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:23.700
will actually remain in network in 2021.

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:28.700
Once inventory balances are
better in check and controlled,

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:31.230
we believe that logistics costs

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:33.080
and inventory freight fulfillment costs

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:34.130
and all of that stuff

00:05:34.130 --> 00:05:37.930
will actually start becoming
a little less of a concern.

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:39.980
- [Narrator] Despite
challenges during the pandemic,

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:42.700
analysts say the future of
the company looks positive.

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:43.720
On March 30th,

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:46.740
Chewy reported its first
quarterly net profit ever

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:50.390
along with a 47% increase
in sales over the past year.

00:05:50.390 --> 00:05:52.870
Analysts expect Chewy to
have its first full year

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:55.330
of profitability in 2021.

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:58.640
But they say that it's rate of
growth will likely slow down.

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:01.200
- This was a major structural shift

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:03.450
in e-commerce penetration
that is, we think,

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:04.780
unlikely to revert.

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:08.300
So we do think 2021
e-commerce growth decelerates

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:10.250
versus what we saw in 2020,

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:11.810
but we don't think you actually give back

00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:12.870
any of the share shift.

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:16.270
So we think this is
structural, this is permanent.

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:17.520
- [Narrator] Experts say the growth

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:20.260
e-commerce companies like
Chewy have experienced

00:06:20.260 --> 00:06:22.030
are likely to be the most significant

00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:23.780
and lasting effects of the pandemic

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:24.970
on the pet care industry.

00:06:24.970 --> 00:06:27.970
(tense tonal music)

